WM Shell: let a host attach the phone PiP menu to any display without a leash.

WSA shows each task in its own Windows window. Its shell attaches the PiP menu as a
shell-root window tagged with the PiP task id, re-attaches it when the task moves
to another display, and forwards input from its own input consumer.

